\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Heal us, Immanuel; hear our prayer;
\par We wait to feel Thy touch:
\par Deep-wounded souls to Thee repair;
\par And, Saviour, we are such.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our faith is feeble, we confess;
\par We faintly trust Thy word:
\par But wilt Thou pity us the less?
\par Be that far from Thee, Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Remember him who once applied
\par With trembling for relief;
\par Lord! I believe! With tears he cried,
\par O help my unbelief!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. She, too, who touched  Thee in the press,
\par And healing virtue stole,
\par Was answered: Daughter, go in peace,
\par Thy faith hath made thee whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Like her, with hopes and fears we come,
\par To touch Thee, if we may:
\par O send us not despairing home,
\par Send none unhealed away.
\par                                Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

